  "question": {
    "text": "If a point <math><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the line segment joining the points <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3,4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8,0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then the distance of <math><mi>R</mi></math> from the origin is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>21</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msqrt><mn>53</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given point <math><mi>R</mi></math> lies on the line segment joining the points <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></math> hence direction ratios of the line<br /><math><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> and <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> must be identical<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0281_e63365afbbb9.png\" style=\"width: 248px; height: 180px;\" /></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext></math> and <math><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, distance from origin <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
